; What the symbols of @CALCULUS@.eo mean, as a transformation into the deep
; embedding of SMT-LIB that the correctness proof is stated against.
;
; This is a stub. Replace it with the semantics of the calculus, either by
; editing here or by rerunning the generator with --semantics pointing at one:
;
;   scripts/new-checker.sh --semantics <path>/@CALCULUS@.eos --force
;
; The SMT-LIB semantics such a file is written against is a second .eos, named
; with --smt-semantics; leaving that one out means the calculus is written
; against whatever base semantics the toolchain supplies.
